  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1251 PM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nTuesday through Sunday:\n\nStrong high pressure centered just north of the Great Lakes \nwill very gradually shift eastward Tuesday through the end of\nthe week. A cooler and much drier airmass is expected across \nsouthern Wisconsin through at least mid-week under the \ninfluence of the high and an upper level troughing pattern. \nBelow normal high and low temps are anticipated through mid- \nweek. \n\nUpper level ridging will attempt to nose into the area from the\nwest later in the week and into the weekend, which should allow\ntemps to return to around normal. Surface high pressure will \nlinger across the Great Lakes into the weekend, which is \nexpected to largely keep conditons dry for southern Wisconsin. \n\nDDV",
